  "stem": "What is the solution to the equation \\(\\sqrt{x + 7} = x - 5\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "9"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Square both sides: \\(x + 7 = x^{2} - 10x + 25\\).",
    "Rearrange: \\(x^{2} - 11x + 18 = 0\\), so \\((x - 9)(x - 2) = 0\\).",
    "Check \\(x = 9\\): \\(\\sqrt{16} = 4\\) and \\(9 - 5 = 4\\). It works.",
    "Check \\(x = 2\\): \\(\\sqrt{9} = 3\\) but \\(2 - 5 = -3\\). It is extraneous. The only solution is \\(9\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\ncands = solve(Eq(x + 7, (x - 5)**2), x)\nassert sorted(cands) == [2, 9]\nsols = solve(Eq(sqrt(x + 7), x - 5), x)\nassert sols == [9]\nassert [Rational(a) for a in spr_answers] == sols",
